---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AboutPlainLead from '../../components/AboutPlainLead.astro';
---

<Layout
  title={'"AI" Reads Human: Human Language Encoding at Machine Speed and the Energy Cost'}
  description={'About: "AI" Reads Human. Software agents exchange data in formats made for people to read. This study measures parse time, token counts, and Apple M5 Max per-process kernel rusage energy (reported_j) across 34 parse and tokenize workloads (measured_j = None, board_metered = false).'}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research topic · work in progress · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      "AI" Reads Human: Human Language Encoding at Machine Speed and the Energy Cost
    </h1>
    <AboutPlainLead id="ai-reads-human" />
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      Software agents pass data to each other in formats made for people to read, such as JSON, YAML, Markdown, XML and CSV. This topic names the extra work that causes (the impedance tax), defines it with units, and measures parse time, token counts across five open tokenizers, and dual-channel Apple M5 Max on-chip <code>reported_j</code> energy across 34 parse and <code>tiktoken</code> workloads on a reproducible 20,000-record corpus (<code>measured_j = None</code>, <code>board_metered = false</code>).
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">In plain words</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Computers and people often use the same written format. That format is easy for people to read, but the computer has to do extra work to read it back.</li>
        <li>Measured via macOS per-process kernel <code>ri_energy_nj</code> (<code>L3</code> <code>reported_j</code>) on Apple M5 Max, reading fixed binary (<code>struct.iter_unpack</code>) cost <code>280.4 nJ/record</code>, versus <code>2,212 nJ/record</code> (<code>7.89×</code>) for stdlib JSON, <code>69,922 nJ/record</code> (<code>249.4×</code>) for C-accelerated YAML, and <code>575,799 nJ/record</code> (<code>2,053.8×</code>) for pure-Python YAML.</li>
        <li>Tokenizing compact JSON with <code>tiktoken</code> (<code>cl100k_base</code>) cost <code>27,679 nJ/record</code> — <code>12.5×</code> the CPU <code>reported_j</code> of <code>json.loads()</code> parsing itself, and <code>2.86×</code> as many tokens for pretty-printed JSON as for CSV. Concurrently, whole-chip <code>IOReport</code> (<code>L2</code>) demonstrated Falsifier 6 co-tenant baseline drift on <code>109 / 170</code> shared-host windows. External wall-meter readings (<code>measured_j</code>) and GPU prefill/decode joules remain open.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/ai-reads-human/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read → /papers/ai-reads-human/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/ai-reads-human.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/living/ai-reads-human/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/30 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Observatory, charts &amp; data → /living/ai-reads-human/
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
